course: dictionary
lesson: 12064
title: Classify: sorting into groups
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To classify something is to sort it into groups by what the things have in common. A group is called a category. «We classify the creatures from the pond into fish, insects and snails.» Each creature goes into the group it fits best.
explain: To classify can also mean deciding which group something belongs to. «The scientist classified the mystery plant as a fern.» She looked at its leaves and stem, then chose the group they matched. Classify as is a useful phrase for this.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so check the context. «The plans were classified, so only the leaders could read them.» Here classified means secret, and only certain people are allowed to see it. The words around it tell you which meaning is right.
fact: Classify is a verb: classify, classifies, classified, classifying.
fact: «Classify» means to sort things into groups or categories by what they have in common.
fact: Scientists classify animals into groups such as mammals, birds and reptiles.
fact: «Classified information» is secret and only for certain people.
fact: «Classified ads» are small adverts sorted into sections, such as jobs or cars.
exercise: «Sam classified the shells into groups by their colour.» What does classified mean here? | *Sorted into groups | Secret and hidden | Counted one by one | Broken into small pieces
exercise: Which group would a dolphin be classified as? | Insect | Fish | *Mammal | Plant
exercise: Which phrase means to decide which group something belongs to? | Classify by colour | Classified ads | *Classify as | Classified information
test: «The librarian classified the books by subject, so all the science books sat together.» What does classified mean here? | Hidden from readers | Read aloud to the class | *Sorted into groups | Lost and never found
test: Mia says a bat is a bird because it flies. Which group should a bat be classified as, and why? | Bird, because it flies | *Mammal, because it has fur and feeds its babies milk | Reptile, because it has scales | Insect, because it is small
exam: «The newspaper printed classified ads for bikes and sofas.» What are the classified ads? | Secret reports for the police | Long stories about sport | Maps of the local town | *Small adverts sorted into sections
